Manually upgrade a kairos node Active image. Does not upgrade the passive image. It upgrades the recovery image when the --recovery flag is passed.

To specify a version, pass it as argument using the --source flag. Passing just the Kairos version as the first argument is no longer supported. If you speficy a positional argument, it will be treated
as a value for the --source flag. Flags go before it: anything after the positional argument is refused.

You can also specify the upgrade image by setting "upgrade.system.uri" for the active image or "upgrade.recovery-system.uri" for the recovery image, in the cloud config.

To pull from a registry served over plain HTTP or presenting an untrusted/self-signed TLS certificate, pass the --allow-insecure-registries flag (or set "upgrade.allow-insecure-registries: true" in the cloud config).

To check what an upgrade would do before running it, pass the --dry-run flag. It resolves the source (including the cloud config), the image size and where the transition image would be written, checks that the image manifest can be fetched from the registry, prints a summary and exits without changing the system.

To retrieve all the available versions, use "kairos agent upgrade list-releases". Use the --registry flag to specify a custom registry to retrieve the versions from, otherwise it will default to quay.io/kairos.

$ kairos agent upgrade list-releases

See https://kairos.io/docs/upgrade/manual/ for documentation.

Usage:
  kairos agent upgrade [flags]
  kairos agent upgrade [command]

Available Commands:
  list-releases List all available releases versions

Flags:
      --allow-insecure-registries[=true|false]   Pull the image from a registry served over plain HTTP or presenting an untrusted/self-signed TLS certificate. Can also be set in the cloud config via "install.allow-insecure-registries" or "upgrade.allow-insecure-registries".
      --boot-entry string                        Specify a systemd-boot entry to upgrade (other than active/passive/recovery). The value should match the name of the '.efi' file.
      --dry-run[=true|false]                     Resolve the upgrade and print a summary of what would be done, without changing the system
      --exclude-path strings                     Path in the new image to leave out of the upgrade, from the image root, e.g. /var/lib/foo or etc/*.conf. A leading / is optional, an excluded directory drops its contents, and * and ? are globs that do not cross /. Can be specified multiple times.
  -h, --help[=true|false]                        help for upgrade
      --image string                             [DEPRECATED] Specify a full image reference, e.g.: quay.io/some/image:tag
      --recovery[=true|false]                    Upgrade recovery
      --source type:address                      Source for upgrade. Composed of type:address. Accepts `file:`,`dir:` `oci:`,or `ocifile:` for the type of source.
                                                 For example `ocifile:/var/share/myimage.tar`, `dir:/tmp/extracted` or `oci:repo/image:tag`

Global Flags:
      --debug[=true|false]               enable debug output [$KAIROS_AGENT_DEBUG]
      --strict-validation[=true|false]   Fail instead of warn on validation errors. [$STRICT_VALIDATIONS]

#
[exit 0]

